post.summary:
Worker declares it has engaged this assignment — the pull-side
`started_at` signal (push-side is the `hire.created` webhook 2xx;
managed agents are stamped at dispatch claim).

RailBalance.description:
Per-rail balance. `available` is rendered as a decimal string so
the client never has to deal with floating-point on a money value;
scale matches the rail's canonical precision (USD = 2, USDC = 6).

SuspensionDisposition.description:
How hard a suspension bites. `Drain` blocks new intake only;
`Halt` also closes every runtime path (dispatch, relay, MCP,
broker mint) and cascade-cancels in-flight work with a refund.

status.description:
`"verified"` when `is_verified` flag is true on the account row;
`"almost_there"` when every gating check passes but the weekly
re-check hasn't stamped the flag yet; `"not_started"` otherwise.
